msgstr "Output:"

msgid "al.scope 接口文档"
msgstr "al.scope API Documentation"

msgid "昇腾处理器包含多种类型的计算单元（例如，用于矩阵运算的 Cube Unit 和用于向量/标量运算的 Vector Unit）。al.scope 允许内核开发者显式地告诉 Triton 编译器，特定代码区域应该目标哪种硬件单元，从而实现更精细的性能调优和资源利用。"
msgstr "The Ascend processor includes multiple types of computing units (e.g., Cube Unit for matrix operations and Vector Unit for vector/scalar operations). `al.scope` allows kernel developers to explicitly tell the Triton compiler which hardware unit a specific code region should target, enabling more fine-grained performance tuning and resource utilization."

msgid "al.scope 是 triton.language.extra.ascend 模块中的一个上下文管理器（Context Manager），专为 Triton 内核中的代码块指定 昇腾硬件的执行模式。"
msgstr "al.scope is a context manager in the triton.language.extra.ascend module, specifically used to specify the execution mode of Ascend hardware for code blocks within a Triton kernel."

msgid "常用值说明"
msgstr "Common Values Description"

msgid "each kernel have 1 scope for cube and vector, inside them they run parallely and there are other syncing operations that declares the sync between both of the scope"
msgstr "Each kernel has one scope for cube and vector, inside which they run in parallel, and there are other synchronization operations that declare the sync between the two scopes."

msgid "Parallel Execution: Operations within cube and vector scopes execute in parallel"
msgstr "Parallel Execution: Operations within cube and vector scopes execute in parallel"

msgid "Single Scope per Type: Each kernel supports one cube scope and one vector scope (?)"
msgstr "Single Scope per Type: Each kernel supports one cube scope and one vector scope (?)"

msgid "Explicit Synchronization: Required for data dependencies between scopes using sync operations"
msgstr "Explicit Synchronization: Required for data dependencies between scopes using sync operations"

msgid "sub_vec_id"
msgstr "sub_vec_id"

msgid "昇腾硬件AIC与AIV核数配比不同（1:N），Triton编程抽象屏蔽了Cube核与Vector核的硬件细节，因此，Triton算子开发者无法控制如何切分数据在N个Vector核间并行处理，由编译器通过AutoSubTiling Pass自动实现。"
msgstr "The ratio of AIC to AIV cores on Ascend hardware varies (1:N). The Triton programming abstraction hides the hardware details of Cube and Vector cores, so Triton operator developers cannot control how data is split for parallel processing across N Vector cores. This is automatically handled by the compiler through the AutoSubTiling Pass."

msgid "sub_vec_id编程接口返回N个Vector核的sub id，允许算子开发者根据vector核sub id决定每个核处理哪些数据。"
msgstr "The `sub_vec_id` programming interface returns the sub IDs of N Vector cores, allowing operator developers to determine which data each core processes based on the vector core sub ID."

msgid "返回值：返回范围为 [0, N) 的 Sub Vector ID，算子开发者可根据该ID决定N个并行Vector核中每个核处理的数据分片"
msgstr "Return value: Returns the Sub Vector ID in the range [0, N). The operator developer can use this ID to determine the data partition processed by each of the N parallel Vector cores."

msgid "入参：无"
msgstr "Input parameters: none"

msgid "仅在AIC和AIV核混合使用场景中有效，不可在纯Cube类算子或者纯Vector类算子中使用，否则会触发编译报错。"
msgstr "Only valid in scenarios where AIC and AIV cores are used together; it cannot be used in pure Cube-type operators or pure Vector-type operators, otherwise a compilation error will be triggered."

msgid "subview"
msgstr "Subview"

msgid "昇腾硬件 A5 支持了定义新视图，仅通过偏移、大小和步幅实现，不复制底层数据。"
msgstr "Ascend hardware A5 supports defining new views, implemented only through offset, size, and stride, without copying the underlying data."

msgid "接口一"
msgstr "Interface One"

msgid "接口二"
msgstr "Interface Two"

msgid "返回值：bl.buffer"
msgstr "Return value: bl.buffer"

msgid "3. 入参说明"
msgstr "3. Input Parameter Description"

msgid "src: buffer -> 源buffer"
msgstr "src: buffer -> source buffer"

msgid "offsets: List[tl.tensor] -> 偏移"
msgstr "offsets: List[tl.tensor] -> offsets"

msgid "sizes: List[tl.constexpr] -> 输出的size"
msgstr "sizes: List[tl.constexpr] -> the size of the output"

msgid "strides: List[tl.constexpr] -> 步长"
msgstr "strides: List[tl.constexpr] -> strides"

msgid "4. 约束说明"
msgstr "4. Constraint Description"

msgid "输入的参数size、offset、stride必须大于0（offset可以是0），不能为负值。"
msgstr "The input parameters `size`, `offset`, and `stride` must be greater than 0 (`offset` can be 0) and cannot be negative."

msgid "size的每一个维度的大小不能大于原buffer的大小。"
msgstr "The size of each dimension of `size` cannot exceed the size of the original buffer."

msgid "子视图的每一个维度的大小不能超过原buffer的大小。"
msgstr "The size of each dimension of a subview cannot exceed the size of the original buffer."

msgid "stride的访问不能超过src的大小，stride所有元素全为1。"
msgstr "The access of stride cannot exceed the size of src, and all elements of stride are 1."

msgid "参数的设置要指明每一个维度的值，参数维度应该和输入buffer的维度保持一致。"
msgstr "The parameter settings must specify the value for each dimension, and the parameter dimensions should be consistent with the dimensions of the input buffer."

msgid "offset必须32字节对齐。"
msgstr "The offset must be 32-byte aligned."

msgid "子视图中最后一个维度的第二行第一个点的偏移必须是32字节对齐。"
msgstr "The offset of the first point in the second row of the last dimension in a subview must be 32-byte aligned."

msgid "解释补充：sizes、strides在使用的时候传入类型：List[tl.constexpr]（注意不要误传tensor，否则会报错-类型不匹配）。offsets补充支持了tensor传入（也可以传入constexpr）"
msgstr "Explanation: When using `sizes` and `strides`, the input type should be `List[tl.constexpr]` (note: do not mistakenly pass a tensor, otherwise an error will occur due to type mismatch). For `offsets`, support for tensor input has been added (constexpr can also be passed)."

msgid "5. 用例示例"
msgstr "5. Usage Examples"

msgid "当不同核之间操作同一块全局内存且可能存在读后写、写后读以及写后写等数据依赖问题时，通过调用该函数来插入同步语句来避免上述数据依赖时可能出现的数据读写错误问题。"
msgstr "When different cores operate on the same global memory and there may be data dependencies such as read-after-write, write-after-read, and write-after-write, call this function to insert synchronization statements to avoid data read/write errors that may occur due to the aforementioned data dependencies."

msgid "2.2 返回值"
msgstr "2.2 Return Value"

msgid "3. 约束"
msgstr "3. Constraints"

msgid "mode可选字符串:all_cube/all_vector/all/all_sub_vector"
msgstr "mode optional string: all_cube/all_vector/all/all_sub_vector"

msgid "event_id范围是[0,15]"
msgstr "The range of event_id is [0, 15]."

msgid "4. 示例"
msgstr "4. Examples"

msgid "al.sync_block_set 接口文档"
msgstr "al.sync_block_set API Documentation"

msgid "面向分离模式的核间同步控制接口。"
msgstr "Inter-core synchronization control interface for separation mode."

msgid "该接口和 sync_block_wait 接口配合使用。使用时需传入核间同步的标记ID(flagId)，每个ID对应一个初始值为0的计数器。执行CrossCoreSetFlag后ID对应的计数器增加1；执行CrossCoreWaitFlag时如果对应的计数器数值为0则阻塞不执行；如果对应的计数器大于0，则计数器减一，同时后续指令开始执行。"
msgstr "This interface is used in conjunction with the `sync_block_wait` interface. When using it, the inter-core synchronization flag ID (`flagId`) must be passed in, where each ID corresponds to a counter with an initial value of 0. After executing `CrossCoreSetFlag`, the counter corresponding to the ID is incremented by 1; when executing `CrossCoreWaitFlag`, if the corresponding counter value is 0, it blocks and does not execute; if the corresponding counter is greater than 0, the counter is decremented by 1, and subsequent instructions begin execution."

msgid "无返回值"
msgstr "No return value"

msgid "4. PIPE 枚举说明"
msgstr "4. PIPE Enumeration Description"

msgid "5. 约束说明"
msgstr "5. Constraint Description"

msgid "sender != receiver"
msgstr "sender != receiver"

msgid "6. 用例示例"
msgstr "6. Use Case Examples"

msgid "al.sync_block_wait 接口文档"
msgstr "al.sync_block_wait API Documentation"

msgid "该接口和 sync_block_set 接口配合使用。使用时需传入核间同步的标记ID(flagId)，每个ID对应一个初始值为0的计数器。执行CrossCoreSetFlag后ID对应的计数器增加1；执行CrossCoreWaitFlag时如果对应的计数器数值为0则阻塞不执行；如果对应的计数器大于0，则计数器减一，同时后续指令开始执行。"
msgstr "This interface is used in conjunction with the `sync_block_set` interface. When using it, you need to pass the inter-core synchronization flag ID (`flagId`), where each ID corresponds to a counter with an initial value of 0. After executing `CrossCoreSetFlag`, the counter corresponding to the ID increments by 1; when executing `CrossCoreWaitFlag`, if the corresponding counter value is 0, it blocks and does not execute; if the corresponding counter is greater than 0, the counter decrements by 1, and subsequent instructions begin execution."

