msgstr "6. Minimum Call Example"

msgid "6.1 C/C++ 示例（已有 func 句柄后）"
msgstr "6.1 C/C++ Example (After Having the func Handle)"

msgid "以下示例假设调用方已通过 CANN runtime 完成 kernel binary 的注册并持有可用的 `func` handle，仅展示调用 `triton_launch_kernel` 的参数组织方式。kernel 注册流程（`rtDevBinaryRegister` / `rtFunctionRegister`）属于 CANN runtime 标准流程，不在本示例范围内。"
msgstr "The following example assumes that the caller has completed the registration of the kernel binary via the CANN runtime and holds an available `func` handle. It only demonstrates how to organize parameters for calling `triton_launch_kernel`. The kernel registration process (`rtDevBinaryRegister` / `rtFunctionRegister`) is part of the standard CANN runtime workflow and is not covered in this example."

msgid "**说明：** 示例中的 `func` 参数是 CANN runtime 注册后的 kernel function handle，获取方式（`rtDevBinaryRegister` / `rtFunctionRegister`）属于 CANN runtime 标准流程。当前仓内 `npu_utils.cpp` 中的 `loadKernelBinary` / `registerKernel` 函数提供了 Python 侧的封装实现，具体 API 签名请以 CANN 头文件（`runtime/kernel.h`）为准。关于这些辅助函数是否可作为公开 API 文档化，请参见[待确认事项](#待确认事项)。"
msgstr "**Note:** The `func` parameter in the example is the kernel function handle registered by the CANN runtime. The method to obtain it (`rtDevBinaryRegister` / `rtFunctionRegister`) follows the standard CANN runtime procedure. The `loadKernelBinary` / `registerKernel` functions in `npu_utils.cpp` within this repository provide Python-side wrapper implementations. For specific API signatures, refer to the CANN header file (`runtime/kernel.h`). Regarding whether these helper functions can be documented as public APIs, please see [Pending Confirmation](#pending-confirmation)."

